#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119610 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/id #uuid "9552ad30-9d46-5884-9877-18ca8842c252" :question/math-academy-id "e-4775" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b},$ given by\n![](images/45/45cefb7311cd5253b76164cc7f2f3ce01b445f0e9061b720865227128b60debe.png)\nIf $\\langle x_1,x_2 \\rangle$ and $\\langle y_1,y_2 \\rangle$ are the solutions to the systems $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ and $L\\mathbf{y}=\\mathbf{b}$ respectively, what is the value of $x_1 \\cdot y_2?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](images/b5/b521c0b31d05de273d0abd37e00b046c0e36ed47ef30d22784a24cace4d676f9.png)\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n![](images/9d/9dcc9f71745cce72ce7e122b3bc8cd7064d05f3be90d712202f42956956ef18e.png)\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=6 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $y_1=6$ and $y_2=4.$ Therefore, \n![](images/90/903fbfe6828526dace264d65baebf58c31e36db8a54e25ed1f3be859e6079ebb.png)\n\n- Next, we solve $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n![](images/dc/dcb234ae13cab2676ea5afa7fde452c870ff5088ff5748342c517bf2a96327a8.png)\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $x_2=-2$ and $x_1=2.$ Therefore, \n![](images/53/53bace542ba4dfd0d7e5e4bf9b6451c7f39502dd1bf24d030f654050629f0e0d.png)\n\nFinally, $x_1 \\cdot y_2 = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119611 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "24bc4954-462b-5066-83d4-8a4a87efc7b7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4777" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $\\mathbf b,$ given by \n![](images/f8/f88cbbb9459dd3b467e6b87d230ad23634461597aa9d8da3e933774273e2ab2f.png)\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $\\mathbf{y}$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](images/77/7704f9285f14f496bb9f1721d188866c9464c585e33235c5cc6eee42e3f3a3eb.png)\n\nWe now solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n![](images/71/712643d674cf8a7a086a9a935659d86bba7bd2fb25f131ec56e798cfc1d538d9.png)\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=2 \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=4 \\\\ {y}_{1}-2{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =2, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =4-{y}_{1} \\\\  & =4-(2) \\\\  & =2, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =1-{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1-(2)+2(2) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n![](images/15/151dc664a131df0f3e13f2997bb1af6d41586b5f4dcf8a1acd1342f85e1b9c92.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119706 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "cbefba9a-eda2-5a8e-8bb5-59ea4175b835" :question/math-academy-id "e-8926" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $\\mathbf b,$ given by \n\n![](images/fd/fd1cf7c3d929fb79576a59d4ef3aebd3f24a0d570c938ab80ebd44c5bd4c238f.png)\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $\\mathbf{y}$ such that \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](images/b5/b521c0b31d05de273d0abd37e00b046c0e36ed47ef30d22784a24cace4d676f9.png)\n\nWe now solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 15 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 66\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=5 \\\\ 15{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=66.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $y_1=5$ and $y_2=-9.$ \n\nTherefore, ![](images/cc/ccb4ab47d3a270cf9545d4f79e6f90b944cf6121fca3752eeee6ddc712fcfdec.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241124 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d4b3937-d636-543e-b0d6-739f7a00e7f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 34\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238719} {:answer/id #uuid "59c3bb80-7b1c-535e-843c-7be8777981fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -34\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238826} {:answer/id #uuid "d6a16e65-a824-55dd-90aa-570d8ce9e4fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239931} {:answer/id #uuid "dbc1e9dc-6f28-50f2-90f2-765e57d990e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 36\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239972} {:answer/id #uuid "ec701eb0-1499-57d0-9f0b-83cacf08003b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d4b3937-d636-543e-b0d6-739f7a00e7f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 34\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238719} :answer-field/id #uuid "06e2738a-d273-5c9d-8b63-8b44a8f24c45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d3a99bb0-e72d-5183-bc18-0817eb820005" :question/math-academy-id "q-105760" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=7 \\\\ -10{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=7$ and ${y}_{2}=34.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 34\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241145 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "253c5bec-a5e7-5fe4-8936-ee84f06ad2cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 70 \\\\ 80\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238380} {:answer/id #uuid "3431ca67-1154-5315-a55d-30d8b6ec10fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -63 \\\\ 81\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238506} {:answer/id #uuid "5467b34d-2f1e-5c78-85dd-2b5382f7e7be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -56 \\\\ 80\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238782} {:answer/id #uuid "b152e191-5d18-598f-a23e-0286d0d7f786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 56 \\\\ -80\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239602} {:answer/id #uuid "c8674c02-d35b-548c-9f92-7fdac92d42e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -70 \\\\ 80\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5467b34d-2f1e-5c78-85dd-2b5382f7e7be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -56 \\\\ 80\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238782} :answer-field/id #uuid "697b8f6f-9b78-510a-bdce-c0f202963523" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "90586eea-75b4-50dc-8971-26e34a9a2816" :question/math-academy-id "q-105934" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=9 \\\\ 7{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=7 \\\\ -9{y}_{1}+{y}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =9, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =7-7{y}_{1} \\\\  & =7-7(9) \\\\  & =-56, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =-1+9{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-1+9(9) \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -56 \\\\ 80\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22f6367b-84f5-5b47-a09a-aa8de2644b8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238362} {:answer/id #uuid "813327d9-1832-51ef-84d1-00133e2f63a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239176} {:answer/id #uuid "8e93b878-423d-5080-a191-f592c8e25cbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{130}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239293} {:answer/id #uuid "b7069b81-e348-5968-b6ae-a411b5b35221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239649} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc34193-52f9-5bb0-a06a-5f9897960a24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7069b81-e348-5968-b6ae-a411b5b35221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239649} :answer-field/id #uuid "54336a57-2806-5ed6-bb5d-a86bbfed1d7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "68b89d00-e814-5d60-8ff8-bbe1b29f01fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-105953" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=5 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=5$ and ${y}_{2}=14.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-7$ and ${x}_{1}=\\frac{26}{7}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{26}{7} \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}=\\frac{26}{7}\\cdot 14=52.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377100 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "122c6d88-8494-5aec-a026-229428468b5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377102} {:answer/id #uuid "a24fc545-7e28-5319-b8ea-0050a0425013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377103} {:answer/id #uuid "565b9eb2-7221-52ec-8a34-db861601dd2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377104} {:answer/id #uuid "66cde035-3c2e-5045-8a57-e62cdfc4c320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377105} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec426d5-6612-5ded-909b-99d6a4c1702f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66cde035-3c2e-5045-8a57-e62cdfc4c320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377105} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa4faae0-0911-57b4-a7e3-89f58f84a03e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf45deeb-ab83-510b-8f67-2f8280e43963" :question/math-academy-id "q-32543" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=1 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =1, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-2+2{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-2+2(1) \\\\  & =0, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =2+{y}_{1}-{y}_{2} \\\\  & =2+(1)-(0) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390757 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "032457e9-02bf-5ad6-9987-99a0689c6243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390759} {:answer/id #uuid "ad2b9196-139c-5abe-8bf3-f21b13bb615e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390760} {:answer/id #uuid "d6722917-7648-59db-8da1-966d52f9d9ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390761} {:answer/id #uuid "9541c84f-6c02-5508-afe7-624da511dbdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390762} {:answer/id #uuid "749e40df-d35d-5ad6-9d4a-9737f8552554" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad2b9196-139c-5abe-8bf3-f21b13bb615e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390760} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e79de7e-b384-5ea6-bb81-dfd5832cccb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390758}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b44ae0d1-f2bc-52f5-a02c-1e4fb0c1d4e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-32561" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=3 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=3$ and ${y}_{2}=3.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=\\frac{3}{2}$ and ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{3}{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{1}=-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 3=-\\frac{9}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302218 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3be1af41-0c7e-535a-9a86-a5c82122dcdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300250} {:answer/id #uuid "89b9efd6-ce79-56d0-af07-0e42c41ffec0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300659} {:answer/id #uuid "98709d57-b5d1-505c-a13b-2435f487b4d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300728} {:answer/id #uuid "b5fc1198-c5b8-53d4-8b4a-c8b8adf38ad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300866} {:answer/id #uuid "b65d5146-dbe1-5221-b3af-8171d063039f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98709d57-b5d1-505c-a13b-2435f487b4d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300728} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ff87f9e-a211-5118-b7af-25e270840e47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301437}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "74c73bef-8f9e-5d05-b33f-448bad8fb053" :question/math-academy-id "q-32570" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-4 \\\\ 2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=-4$ and ${y}_{2}=2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-4{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3}$ and ${x}_{1}=2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-4+3(-\\frac{2}{3})=-6.$"}]}
